From 8e7d820301e30517ef9ddba6103c098228312f44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 06:33:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] Hoy waits for her own progress before offering a day
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After a sign-in on a new phone, or again after her session expired, the
store's progress is either a fresh Day 1 or empty until /api/me/paths
lands. Hoy (and the Atlas "Continue") read that as "Semana 1 · Día 1 ·
Empezar el día 1": a member in week 2 was offered Day 1, forever if the
read failed, and answering it rewrote the Day 1 answers she gave weeks ago.

The store now records whose progress it holds (progressSyncedFor): set by
a server read made for the signed-in account, or by a brand-new account's
own start in finalizeOnboarding, persisted with the progress, cleared by
accountReset. Today's entry is null until it names her; Hoy shows a
placeholder while the read is on its way and the existing "No pudimos
cargar esto ahora…" + "Reintentar" if it failed. A read made for another
account is never applied. Stores persisted before the field count as the
last account's, so an offline first launch after the update still works.

Tests: progressSync.test.ts (through the real store), accountState.test.ts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MRH1FyKGTN3zfVru4KrGk9
