From 55d5c43d1bca3bb5031b9bf8c3221654b98d1578 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 06:54:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] Tell a free account the truth at the week-2 gate
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A free account that closed week 1 read «La semana 2, Wuzhen, se abre
mañana»; the next morning «Empezar el día 1» opened the membership screen,
which said «Tu camino gratis está listo. … Continúa con el camino que
elegimos para ti.» with nothing on sale, and «Continuar» went back to the
same Hoy: a loop with no way forward. Beta testers created after the last
beta-grant sweep (or whose 90-day grant ends) land exactly here.

- Hoy no longer promises a membership week to an account without one
  (promisesNextWeek), and a locked week's line carries the path page's
  existing «· Premium» badge.
- The membership screen, reached from a locked week with nothing to buy,
  says «Las membresías no están a la venta en este momento.» and what the
  free plan holds (freeNoteWithArea), with «Contactar a soporte» to ask.
  All existing, approved strings.

The way through for testers is still a beta grant (admin, or
scripts/grant-beta-all.sql re-run after new sign-ups): an owner action.

Tests: todayEntry.test.ts (promisesNextWeek).

