From f248a9bf624e96fdb52b461f53e6a1fb141dd529 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 06:57:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] Ask again for what failed when the phone is back online
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After a launch without signal, everything that failed to load stayed
failed once the connection returned: the CMS paths the day screen walks,
Hoy's «Para hoy» guide and rhythm, the assessments and the app's switches.
React Query is not told about the phone's connection (onlineManager has no
listener in React Native), and SessionSync only re-asked for the session
and /api/me. Hoy kept a missing guide and the bundled copy of the paths
until a screen remounted or she pulled to refresh.

On the way back online (expo-network, the same signal as the offline
banner), SessionSync now refetches every query on screen whose last read
failed (reconnectRefetch): nothing that worked is re-read and nothing off
screen is fetched.

Tests: query.test.ts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MRH1FyKGTN3zfVru4KrGk9
