From 2c22c4ad301191c819f12ff179e7e6e2a95a7bf7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:14:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] Day screen: keep her words on skip and on refusals,
 never offer a day the server will refuse
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Found and reproduced in the browser (beta-fixes, 3 Nov):

- «Prefiero pasar» threw away what she had typed on the step. Her input is
  now kept as the step's draft (saved at once, not lost to the debounce), so
  going back to the step brings it back. It is still cleared over an answer
  she already holds, as before.
- An answer the server refused for good (a week that locked under her, a
  step the content no longer has, a shape it no longer takes) was dropped by
  the queue with her words, while the completion screen said they were saved.
  The flush now hands such an entry over first (onDropped) and the store puts
  her words back in that step as a kept answer: the step opens with them and a
  line saying they could not be saved, and the completion line says so.
- A day finished offline late in the evening, synced after midnight: the
  phone opened the next day, the server stamped the first day at upload and
  refused the next one (403 day_locked). The day gate now counts a finished
  day whose answers are still queued from now, as the server will.
- Money Día 1 still drew the old feelings-check-in weather (stressed, calm,
  unsure) beside its income options; the art now belongs to the feelings step
  only.
- The return line read «De vuelta en la vuelta.» at the generic stop «La
  vuelta»; proposed «De nuevo en la vuelta.».
- The reflection placeholder was 3.4:1 on the card and the paper; it uses the
  readable secondary ink now (5.9:1), and sits above the paper art on web.

New Spanish strings are proposals for native review.

