 waits for her progress before the gate
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Composition of the two branches on Hoy's entry:

- A refused answer is kept under the step's draft key as { kept, refused }
  (beta-session-fixes, onDropped). draftHasWords only knew StepDraft, so
  Hoy resumed that day without «Guardamos lo que escribiste» over words
  the phone was keeping. It now reads a kept answer by its words.
- The progress-ready rule and the gate are one pure step
  (todayEntryWhenReady): no door before her progress is read, whatever
  the gate says; once it is, a day still queued waits counted from now.
  Tests pin both orders against dayGateFor(..., unsynced).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
